netbird-lite changes to wireguard-lwip (https://github.com/smartalock/wireguard-lwip, BSD-3-Clause),
relative to upstream commit c54f20d (src/ directory). All other vendored files are unmodified.
To reproduce the vendored copy, run "patch -p1 < NBL-PATCH.diff" in a copy of upstream src/.

  - listen_port == 0: no UDP socket; packets go to nbl_wg_transport_send() and come in through
    wireguardif_network_rx() (transport = NetBird relay)
  - decrypted packets are passed to netif->input instead of ip_input() so the inbound ACL runs first
  - IPv4 helpers for IPv4-only fields so the code builds with dual-stack lwIP; IPv6 cookie branch disabled
  - debug printf() calls removed
  - WIREGUARD_MAX_PEERS / WIREGUARD_MAX_SRC_IPS can be overridden at build time
  - the timer never takes the netif link down: lwIP routes around link-down netifs, so VPN
    traffic would leave unencrypted via the default route while no peer has a session

